# Copy to `.env` in this directory and edit. Docker Compose reads it ONLY when it CREATES
# a container: editing a value has no effect on an already-running one. Force a recreate:
#     cd transfer/obelisk/docker && docker compose up -d --force-recreate
#
# ============================ GENERATE IT, DO NOT COPY IT ==============================
# Every value below the Identity heading is HOST-SPECIFIC, and a stale one fails in a way
# that points somewhere else entirely. Copying this file from another machine has already
# cost one debugging session per value:
#
#   wrong REPO_ROOT   -> docker CREATES the missing path as an empty root-owned directory
#                        rather than erroring, so the container's workspace is empty and
#                        colcon reports `PermissionError: 'log'`. Reads as permissions.
#   wrong UID/GID     -> bind-mounted files come out owned by a uid the host user cannot
#                        clean up, and colcon fails on directories it created itself.
#   wrong INPUT_GID   -> the joystick is present, readable by root, and silently invisible
#                        to the container user.
#   no ~/.gitconfig   -> not a value here, but the same shape: compose mounts it, docker
#                        creates the missing target as a DIRECTORY, and every git call
#                        inside the container then fails with "Is a directory", which
#                        surfaces as a FetchContent clone failure. Fix with `touch
#                        ~/.gitconfig` before the first bring-up.
#
# So generate it for THIS machine instead of editing a copy (run from this directory):
#
#   cat > .env <<EOF
#   USER=$(id -un)
#   UID=$(id -u)
#   GID=$(id -g)
#   REPO_ROOT=$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)
#   ROBOT_RL_ROOT=$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)/transfer/obelisk
#   INPUT_GID=$(getent group input | cut -d: -f3)
#   DIALOUT_GID=$(getent group dialout | cut -d: -f3)
#   OBK_JETSON_HOST=unitree@192.168.123.164
#   OBK_JETSON_CONTAINER=zed_depth
#   EOF
#   touch ~/.gitconfig
#
# The values below are one machine's, kept only to show the SHAPE of each. They are wrong
# for yours.

# --- Identity -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Must match your host user, or bind-mounted files come out owned by the wrong uid.
#     id -un ; id -u ; id -g
USER=zolkin
UID=1000
GID=1000

# --- Paths ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ROBOT_RL_ROOT is the obelisk workspace (transfer/obelisk). REPO_ROOT is the REPO root and
# is what actually gets mounted: the controller imports transfer/deploy (shared with the
# MuJoCo sim2sim) and the world config loads transfer/sim/robots/g1/*.xml, neither of which
# exists inside the container if only transfer/obelisk is mounted.
REPO_ROOT=/home/zolkin/AmberLab/Project-Isaac-RL/sprout
ROBOT_RL_ROOT=/home/zolkin/AmberLab/Project-Isaac-RL/sprout/transfer/obelisk

# --- Device access --------------------------------------------------------------------
# HOST group ids, so the non-root container user can read the joystick and the serial port
# without `sudo chmod 666`. These are host-specific -- look them up:
#     getent group input   | cut -d: -f3
#     getent group dialout | cut -d: -f3
INPUT_GID=107
DIALOUT_GID=20

# --- Multi-machine DDS (optional) ---------------------------------------------------------
# Leave UNSET for a single-box run: Cyclone's default multicast discovery needs no config,
# which is why nothing here has ever set this. Set it only when the MuJoCo world runs on
# another machine and discovery does not cross the link -- wifi with client isolation is the
# usual reason. Copy cyclonedds.xml.example to cyclonedds.xml, list the OTHER box as a peer
# (on BOTH boxes), and point at it here. Verify with scripts/net_check.sh.
# CYCLONEDDS_URI=file:///home/zolkin/sprout/transfer/obelisk/docker/cyclonedds.xml

# --- Jetson (depth camera) --------------------------------------------------------------
# ssh target and container name for the ZED depth node, read INSIDE the obk container by
# scripts/lib/obk_launch.sh. Needs minipc->jetson pubkey auth reachable from in there.
OBK_JETSON_HOST=unitree@192.168.123.164
OBK_JETSON_CONTAINER=zed_depth

# TF32 off (0) or on (1) for every CUDA matmul in both networks. LEAVE UNSET for the driver
# default, which is ON for Ampere and later and is what 1 reproduces (measured identical).
#
# It matters because TF32 makes the generator's plan GPU-ARCHITECTURE dependent: replaying one
# recorded stream through the same graph and the same onnxruntime, an x86 desktop and a Jetson
# Thor disagree by 1.37e-2 with it on and 1.60e-5 with it off on both. Everything upstream of
# the network stays bit-identical. Turning it off costs the Thor 20.9 -> 34.3 ms per plan (the
# desktop barely notices, 14.1 -> 14.8), so it competes with the re-plan deadline. A MIXED
# setting across two machines is the worst case of the three.
# NVIDIA_TF32_OVERRIDE=1
